  "summary": "A San Jose police officer was fired after allegedly using Flock ALPR data on a personal device to locate a domestic violence victim's vehicle and sharing the location with a relative who was the suspect. The department has restricted ALPR access on personal devices, admonished officers, and is testing new smart auditing tools; the case was referred to POST for decertification.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The officer, while off duty, used a personal device to perform the unauthorized automatic license plate reader search, related to a domestic violence matter involving family members",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "After finding the victim's vehicle, the officer shared the location with the suspect, who is a relative of the officer",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The department has now restricted automatic license plate reader and other sensitive law enforcement systems from being accessed on personal devices.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "In addition to current monthly ALPR audits, the department is testing new smart auditing tools that go even further to flag possible access without a lawful purpose.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
